⛔ WHAT THIS PLAN EXPECTED AND MEASURED FALSE
---------------------------------------------
The plan predicted run 1 would "exit 1 with EXACTLY the stale-ratchet defects for
FILES_FLOOR (46 > 45) and ARMS_FLOOR (N > 369)". IT DID NOT. `run.mjs`'s gate
paths are `if (annotatedFiles < filesFloor)` and `if (bitingArms < armsFloor)`,
so a floor BELOW the corpus is invisible to the runner BY CONSTRUCTION — run 1
exited 0 with `✅ No defects` on stale-low floors. The stale direction is caught
one layer up, in `src/__tests__/mutation-runner-floors.test.ts`. Both readings
are recorded below, because "separated in both directions" is only true of this
ratchet if you name WHICH LAYER reports each direction.


